Foundation-model embeddings are written as a BIDS derivative dataset of NetCDF files, one dataset per model. A file holds one representation of the model's output, named by its suffix (`tokenembeddings`, `windowembeddings`, `channelembeddings`, `patchembeddings`, `covembeddings`, listed in `EMBEDDING_VIEWS`), and the `desc` entity names the processing, e.g. `desc-baseRandomEaCoral`. `write_recording_embeddings` writes every view of one recording, all its conditions in one file in epoch order, after refusing results that differ in model, settings, views or channels, non-finite values and an epoch number seen twice; a file records its extraction settings as the JSON attribute `config` (keys in `EMBEDDING_CONFIG_KEYS`, CamelCase as BIDS recommends) and their hash `config_hash`, its recording's source as a BIDS URI, and the channels the model saw. `embedding_path` names a recording's file or a dataset-level one and returns its `BIDSPath`. `write_embedding_dataset` writes `dataset_description.json` (BIDS 1.10.1, `DatasetLinks`), `README.md`, `descriptions.tsv` and `descriptions.json`, `.bidsignore` and a JSON sidecar for each dataset-level file; the BIDS validator finds no error in such a dataset. `write_embedding_manifest` records a label's skipped and failed recordings in `desc-<label>_manifest.json`. Every file is replaced atomically, so jobs may write into one dataset at once. Removed: the NPZ embedding API (`save_embedding_derivative`, `save_embedding_outputs`, `validate_embedding_derivative`, `embedding_sidecar_path`, `discover_embedding_derivatives`, `embedding_observation_id`, `load_embedding_derivatives`, `combined_embedding_table_path`, `load_combined_embedding_table`, `write_embedding_dataset_description`) and its combined parquet and CSV tables.
